### UPDATE 'read' VALUE (Ex-23)

### Login as the reading-list owner (replace with valid credentials)
# @name loginOwner
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "barrybee@yahoo.com",
  "password": "secret"
}

### Inspect the user's reading list to grab a valid readingList.id
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/2

### Valid Path (200 OK): Mark reading-list entry as read using owner's token
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/readinglists/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.token}}

{
  "read": true
}

### Verify GET /api/users/:id now reflects "read": true
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/2

### Guard Clause Test (401 Unauthorized): Missing Authorization header
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/readinglists/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "read": true
}

### Guard Clause Test (404 Not Found): Non-existent reading-list entry id
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/readinglists/9999
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.token}}

{
  "read": true
}

### Guard Test (400 Bad Request): Non-boolean value for "read"
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/readinglists/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.token}}

{
  "read": "yes"
}

### Login as a DIFFERENT user to test ownership enforcement
# @name loginOtherUser
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "deanbug@yahoo.com",
  "password": "secret"
}

### Guard Test (403 Forbidden): Authenticated user trying to modify someone else's entry
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/readinglists/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOtherUser.response.body.token}}

{
  "read": false
}


